@* TextArea's Overview, written by hand after TextField's and the selection Overviews: rows,
   growing with a count (previewed in each mode), required with a length, and states.
   Accessibility and See also come from the doc comment. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>A text area takes its label, hint, required mark and limits from the model, as a <Anchor Href="docs/components/text-field">TextField</Anchor> does. Use a text field for one line, such as a name or a title.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Rows and placeholder</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>Rows</Code> for how many lines show (4 by default); longer text scrolls, and people can drag the corner to make it taller.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="text-area-rows" />
<TextBlock>A placeholder disappears as people type, so keep anything they need while writing in the <Code>Hint</Code>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Growing, with a count</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>AutoGrow</Code> to grow with the text from <Code>Rows</Code> up, and <Code>ShowCount</Code> to show "n / max" under the field, against the limit from <Code>[StringLength]</Code>, <Code>[MaxLength]</Code> or <Code>MaxLength</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="text-area-count" />
<TextBlock>Growing is CSS (<Code>field-sizing</Code>), so it works with JavaScript off in browsers that support it; others keep the scroll bar and the corner to drag. The count needs a limit, and the browser stops typing at it.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Required, with a length</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>[Required]</Code> and <Code>[StringLength]</Code> with a <Code>MinimumLength</Code> for the rules, and their <Code>ErrorMessage</Code> for the words the browser and the server show.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="text-area-feedback" />
<TextBlock>The browser checks the minimum only on text someone has typed, so the validator's check after posting is the one to rely on; it also catches text that arrives too long, from a crafted post.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Sizes, read-only and disabled</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>Size</Code> to line up with buttons and other fields, <Code>ReadOnly</Code> for text that posts but can't change, and <Code>Disabled</Code> for text that doesn't post.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="text-area-states" />
<TextBlock>Read-only text can still be selected and copied, and it posts like any other, so a crafted post can change it: check it on the server if it matters. A disabled field posts nothing, so after a static post its property is null: keep its value on the server rather than saving it from the post.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        @* Label, required mark and limits from the model. *@
        <TextArea @bind-Value="Model!.Description" />

        @* A short bio that grows and counts toward its [StringLength]. *@
        <TextArea @bind-Value="Model!.Bio" Rows="2" AutoGrow ShowCount
                  Hint="Up to 160 characters, shown on your profile." />
        """;
}
